ether  he's pretty chill and has an easygoing  laid-back charm about him that's just  what Belle could do with after her  tumultuous experience being held captive  in the beasts castle she did dream up  there being more than her provincial  life and we're not totally convinced  Erika's worldly enough for her but he  did go on voyages across the sea so he  could take Belle on ocean adventures to  unexplored lands and they could immerse  themselves in a whole new world together  you know it definitely would be a whole  new world watching old-fashioned Golden  Age princesses with a modern-day man and  that's exactly what we've done with our  last entry Snow White or aurora with  Roger Radcliffe Snow White in Aurora  have lots in common they both love  animals and they both love to sing you  know who else loves to sing and who else  loves animals specifically dogs that is  Roger from 101 Dalmatians that's who  he's a songwriter and a pet owner and  we'd reckon he'd be a much more  interesting match for either one of  these Golden Age princesses  they each ended up with a prince that  didn't have much character Deb would  they have gotten bored there's no chance  of that with Roger and all those dogs  around we don't reckon either Aurora or  Snow White could deal with a man who  didn't have old-fashioned manners and  Roger actually does for all his quirks  when he first meets Anita and they end  up falling in the pond  he's as chivalrous as they come we could  actually see Cinderella with Roger too  given her love of singing but we think  it's enough to have two princesses vying  for him if Aurora gave up on Roger we  could see her being happy with Prince  Eric he has that balance of adventure  and reliability and if Snow White didn't  end up with Roger we could totally see  her with Prince Adam aka the bees so  there you have it our take on the  characters the Disney Princesses should  have married did we get it right which  alternate matches do you have for your  favor